{"Title":"An Act establishing a sick leave bank for Paul O'Brien, an employee of the Trial Court of the Commonwealth","BillNumber":"H4083","DocketNumber":"HD4532","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"CMG1","Name":"Colleen M. Garry","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/CMG1","ResponseDate":"2023-08-17T11:52:29.237"},"Cosponsors":[{"Id":"CMG1","Name":"Colleen M. Garry","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/CMG1","ResponseDate":"2023-08-17T11:52:29.2366667"},{"Id":"EDJ0","Name":"Edward J. Kennedy","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/EDJ0","ResponseDate":"2023-08-21T10:40:08.0833333"}],"JointSponsor":null,"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/H4083/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Bill","Pinslip":"By Representative Garry of Dracut, a petition (subject to Joint Rule 12) of Colleen M. Garry and Edward J. Kennedy for legislation to establish a sick leave bank for Paul O'Brien, an employee of the Trial Court.  The Judiciary.","DocumentText":"\tNotwithstanding any general or special law to the contrary, the trial court of the commonwealth shall establish a sick leave bank for Paul O’Brien, an employee of the trial court. Any employee of the trial court may voluntarily contribute 1 or more sick, personal or vacation days to the sick leave bank for use by Paul O’Brien. If Paul O’Brien terminates employment with the trial court or requests to dissolve the sick leave bank, any remaining time in the sick leave bank shall be transferred to the trial court paid leave bank. Sick leave bank days shall not be used for absences unrelated to the illness or disability that necessitated the establishment of the sick leave bank as determined by the trial court. \r\n","EmergencyPreamble":"Whereas, The deferred operation of this act would tend to defeat its purpose, which is to  establish forthwith a sick leave bank for a certain employee of the trial court of the commonwealth, therefore it is hereby declared to be an emergency law, necessary for the immediate preservation of the public convenience.\r\n\r\n","RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[],"CommitteeRecommendations":[{"Action":"Suspend Rules","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"H33","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/H33"},"Votes":[]},{"Action":"Favorable","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J19","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J19"},"Votes":[]},{"Action":"Place in OD","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"H52","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/H52"},"Votes":[]},{"Action":"Correctly Drawn","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"H36","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/H36"},"Votes":[]},{"Action":"Correctly Drawn","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"S31","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/S31"},"Votes":[]}],"Amendments":[]}